cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite the MSc thesis below."
title: >-
  Classification of Multispectral & Thermal UAV Images with DeepLab v3:
  presentation at the ArcGIS User Conference Greece - Cyprus 2026
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Koroniadis
    given-names: Nikolaos
    affiliation: "University of the Aegean, Department of Geography"
abstract: >-
  Bilingual (EL/EN), offline reveal.js presentation given at the ArcGIS User
  Conference Greece - Cyprus 2026 (Athens, 22 October 2026). It presents an
  MSc thesis comparing a 7-band (multispectral + nDSM + thermal) versus an RGB
  semantic-segmentation pipeline (DeepLabV3 + PointRend / ResNet-101) on UAV
  imagery of Pamfila, Lesvos (GSD 4.52 cm). The advantage is shown to be
  driven by geometry (nDSM) and heat (LWIR) rather than spectrum.
keywords:
  - remote sensing
  - semantic segmentation
  - convolutional neural networks
  - UAV
  - multispectral
  - thermal
  - nDSM
  - DeepLabV3
  - PointRend
  - GIS
  - ArcGIS
